<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh Jan copper output down 10 pct mth/mth.</title>
<headline>Kazakh Jan copper output down 10 pct mth/mth.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakhstan's January copper output fell 10.1 percent to 19,500 tonnes on December 1996 levels and was 20.2 percent down on year-ago levels, the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It gave the following data for non-ferrous metal production (all figures in tonnes):</p>
<p>				     Jan '97	 Dec '96	Jan '96</p>
<p> Copper				19,533	 21,717	24,476</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	     -10.1	 +14.5	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	     -20.2	 -14.7	   n/a</p>
<p> Zinc				   14,027	15,309	12,721</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change		-8.4	  -2.2	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	     +10.3	 +21.1	   n/a</p>
<p> Lead				    3,392	 6,378	 5,637</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	     -46.8	  +9.4	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	     -39.8	 +67.8	   n/a</p>
<p> Bauxite			     181,600     304,300     251,000</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	     -40.3	 +13.8	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	     -27.6	  +8.9	   n/a</p>
<p> Alumina				91,955	93,974	89,498</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change		-2.1	  +3.2	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change		+2.7	  +0.9	   n/a</p>
<p> Titanium				1,500	 1,212	 0,901</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	     +23.8	  -2.2	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	     +66.5	 +25.6	   n/a</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
